{
  "case_id": "2009-09-367",
  "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0000-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nPAMELA S. KARLAN, ESQ., Stanford, California; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nTOBY J. HEYTENS, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me. Is your argument that if the district court -- for whatever reason, unlikely as it may be -- starts a hearing the day after the rest of the sentence was imposed and has to continue that hearing for 91 days before it can render a judgment --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KARLAN: No. If I understand your question correctly, the district court has imposed sentence on day one announcing imprisonment. Any time during the next 90 days, it has a power to set a date and make final determination of the restitution amount."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HEYTENS: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: To begin by addressing the question just raised by Justice Stevens, the government agrees that we are not aware of any cases that directly confront this finality question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry, that's 60 days after the restitution order has been issued. Am I -- MR. HEYTENS: I believe that's incorrect, Your Honor. The provision that we\u2019re referring to, subsection (d)(5), is reproduced on page 6A of the appendix to the government's brief. It's the, I believe, second sentence of (d)(5) that we\u2019re discussing right now that states: \"If the victim subsequently discovers further losses, the victim shall have 60 days after the discovery of those losses in which to petition the court for an amended restitution order.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Let me see if I understand this. He has 14 days to appeal that. And if he doesn't do that, then later within the 90 days or even after the 90 days, a sentence of restitution is imposed, he can -- he can appeal that sentence of restitution, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Can the (o) -- you remember -- you know what I'm referring to by (o)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So if the -- I didn't understand the answer. If the sentence is not imposed without unnecessary delay, the consequence is that there can be no sentence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Before you do that, tell me what the government appeal would consist of. The 90 days has expired --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And you -- you tell me the court -- the court has no ability to impose restitution after 90 days."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's the use of appealing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Karlan",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the judgment of August 8th became final."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Karlan",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But the -- but -- but, Your Honor, if the government appeals an illegal sentence, that sentence can be corrected and the new mandate from the court of appeals saying you erred in not imposing mandatory restitution starts the 90-day clock again."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, what blocks the reading -- what blocks the reading I just gave?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Karlan",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The principle that there must be one sentence that determines each of the punishments for a particular crime."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-09-367",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "06eb27e60dcd402137b83fe6750143bd2bae691d4e746efff629c4830aa01cfd",
      "evidence_id": "ev-06eb27e60dcd-0003-0008",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
